    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# WHAT THIS WORKFLOW DOES\n## Every day it visits 7 public sources and saves date-stamped JSONL files to disk.\n---\n## 1. TRIGGERS\n### Cron · Daily 05:00 — arXiv, Hugging Face, GitHub, PyPI, npm, USPTO\n### OpenAlex WEEKLY — OpenAlex only, reads pillars.json from disk\n### TEMP CRON / Webhook temp-debug / Test — leftovers, not entry points\n---\n## 2. KEYWORDS\n### Pillar Keywords is the ONLY place to edit what we search for.\n### The 5 pillars: self-hosted-vs-saas · temporal-memory · retrieval-engines · data-persistence · stack-structure\n### Every leg reads from it — change it there, everything follows.\n---\n## 3. EACH LEG = 3 STEPS\n### Ask the website (HTTP) → clean it up (Code) → save a file (Write)\n### Files land in data/<source>/raw/<pillar>-<date>.jsonl\n---\n## 4. VALIDATE, THEN GATE\n### Every leg ends at a Validate node producing ok / errorCount / errors\n### The 5 scored legs merge, then Gate makes ONE decision for the whole run\n### USPTO and OpenAlex skip the Merge — Gate still judges OpenAlex\n---\n## 5. THE EXIT\n### Gate → Route: clean batch goes straight to Databricks\n### Any failure → Slack asks a human: Approve Upload / Cancel Execution\n### Approve uploads the healthy legs; Cancel ends the run, nothing written\n---\n## 6. GOTCHAS\n### Merge waits for ALL inputs — never route a second trigger through it\n### USPTO bypasses Gate on purpose: discovery feed, must never block scored legs\n### HF search= only matches single words (hf: 'graph', not 'graph database')\n### WriteBinaryFile overwrites — filenames must carry pillar + date and a package name\n### Scoped npm names (@scope/name) must be sanitised the same way in write and validate\n### Gate returns ONE summary item when blocked, not one item per leg\n---\n## WHY n8n AT ALL\n### Databricks Free Edition has no outbound internet, so n8n fetches, then uploads via the Databricks node",
        "height": 824,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky_readme",
      "name": "READ ME · How this works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-800, 144]
    },
